---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const marketSignals = [
  "Scotland became the first UK nation to legalise alkaline hydrolysis in March 2026",
  "The UK Government welcomed the Law Commission's consultation on legalising terramation and water cremation in June 2025",
  "Resomation providers are preparing to operate in the UK",
  "The Church of England is considering its position on human composting",
  "Terramation UK has campaigned on this since 2022",
];

const assets = [
  {
    title: "Audience and education",
    description:
      "The reference library people in the UK land on when they search for human composting, what it costs, and whether it is legal yet.",
    includes: [
      "Long-form explainers on the process, science, and costs",
      "Ongoing coverage of UK legislation as it moves",
      "Organic search visibility in a category with few credible voices",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Provider directory",
    description:
      "Find Sustainable Funerals is the discovery layer for natural burial, water cremation, and eco-focused funeral providers — and it already carries commercial inventory.",
    includes: [
      "High-intent visitors comparing sustainable funeral options",
      "Featured listings, category sponsorship, and sponsored content",
      "Direct relationships with providers across the sector",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Demand signal",
    description:
      "A register of interest from people who want human composting the moment it becomes available, held separately from the campaign mailing list.",
    includes: [
      "Names and regions gathered ahead of legalisation",
      "An early read on where UK demand is concentrated",
      "A campaign list of supporters following the legislation",
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="For Investors | Terramation UK"
  description="Human composting is not yet legal in England and Wales. Terramation UK has been building the audience, education, and provider relationships for the category since 2022."
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span class="breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <span aria-current="page">For Investors</span>
      </nav>
      <h1>Investing in what comes next</h1>
      <p class="page-header__sub">
        Human composting is not a legal end-of-life choice in England and Wales yet. Since 2022 we have been building
        the audience, the education layer, and the provider relationships that will matter when it is.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="advertise-hero">
        <div class="advertise-hero__content">
          <p class="advertise-hero__eyebrow">Why now</p>
          <h2>A category that is about to exist</h2>
          <p>
            End-of-life provision in the UK has barely changed in a century. That is now moving: Scotland has opened a
            new category, England and Wales are consulting, and the providers who will serve that market are already
            positioning. Terramation UK has been campaigning and raising awareness here throughout.
          </p>
          <div class="advertise-hero__actions">
            <a href="mailto:info@terramation.uk?subject=Investor%20enquiry" class="btn btn--primary">
              Email us about investing
            </a>
            <a href="/find-sustainable-funerals/" class="btn btn--outline advertise-hero__secondary">
              See what we have built
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="advertise-hero__card">
          <p class="advertise-hero__card-label">Market signals</p>
          <ul class="advertise-signal-list">
            {marketSignals.map((signal) => (
              <li>{signal}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tinted">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__eyebrow">Where we are today</span>
        <h2 class="section__title">What we have built</h2>
        <p class="section__subtitle">
          Three assets, built ahead of the market rather than after it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="advertise-grid">
        {assets.map((asset) => (
          <article class="advertise-card">
            <h3>{asset.title}</h3>
            <p class="advertise-card__description">{asset.description}</p>
            <ul class="advertise-card__list">
              {asset.includes.map((item) => (
                <li>{item}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <span class="section__eyebrow">The thesis</span>
      <h2 style="margin-block-end:var(--space-6);">Where this goes</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Human composting in the UK is currently a question people research rather than a service they can buy. That
          makes education the entry point, and education is what we have spent the last four years building. People
          arrive with a question about the process, the cost, or the law, and they arrive early — often years before a
          decision.
        </p>
        <p>
          Those same people need to find providers. Find Sustainable Funerals is the discovery layer we built for the
          adjacent options that <em>are</em> legal today — natural burial, water cremation, eco-focused funeral
          services — and it is already commercially active through listings and sponsorship. It is the mechanism that
          would carry human composting providers the day they exist.
        </p>
        <p>
          Between the two sits the register of interest: people telling us, unprompted, that they want this when it is
          available, and where in the UK they are. That is demand captured before the market opens.
        </p>
        <p>
          Scotland has now legalised alkaline hydrolysis. If England and Wales follow the direction the Law Commission
          consultation points in, a category appears with an established audience, a working directory, and a waiting
          list already attached to it. We are early, deliberately, and we are talking to investors who understand why
          that timing matters.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tinted">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <div class="directory-cta">
        <h2>Who we would like to hear from</h2>
        <p>
          Angels and funds working in climate, deathtech, or consumer. Operators who have built regulated consumer
          services from scratch. Strategic partners already inside the funeral sector. If the category interests you,
          we would rather know you now than introduce ourselves later.
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:info@terramation.uk?subject=Investor%20enquiry" class="btn btn--primary">
          Email us about investing
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="investor-disclaimer">
        Terramation UK is not currently raising. Nothing on this page is an offer or invitation to invest, or a
        financial promotion under section 21 of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000. It is an introduction for
        investors who want to follow the category as it develops.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
